-- title:
--   Extending a multiplicative, K-linearly coherent map on a generating monoid
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and let $L$, $L'$ be fields equipped with $K$-algebra structures. Let $G \subseteq L$ be a subset with $1 \in G$ that is closed under multiplication, and let $\theta : L \to L'$ be any function which is multiplicative on $G$, i.e. $\theta(xy) = \theta(x)\theta(y)$ for all $x, y \in G$, and which respects the $K$-linear relations among elements of $G$: for every finitely supported function $c : L \to K$ whose support is contained in $G$, if $\sum_{x} c(x)\,x = 0$ in $L$ then $\sum_{x} c(x)\,\theta(x) = 0$ in $L'$. Let $F$ be an intermediate field of $L/K$ equal to the $K$-subfield $K(G)$ of $L$ generated by $G$. Assume there is an element $x_0$ of $F$ whose image in $L$ lies in $G$ and is such that $\theta(x_0)$ is transcendental over $K$, and assume that $F$ is algebraic over the intermediate field of $F/K$ generated by $x_0$. Then there exists a homomorphism of $K$-algebras $\Theta : F \to L'$ with $\Theta(x) = \theta(x)$ for every $x \in F$ whose image in $L$ lies in $G$.
--
--   This is a general field-theoretic extension criterion: a map defined on a multiplicative generating set, multiplicative there and compatible with all $K$-linear relations, extends to the generated field provided that field is algebraic over one generator with transcendental image. It is used in the construction of a $K$-algebra homomorphism on the function field of a modular curve out of a map on $q$-expansions, via [`ModularCurve.exists_algHom_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_coe_eq_div_of_map_eq_smul_qExpansion_slash`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_algHom_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_coe_eq_div_of_map_eq_smul_qExpansion_slash).
